Package: NonlinearBSS
Type: Package
Title: Nonlinear Blind Source Separation
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mika", "Sipilä", email = "mika.e.sipila@jyu.fi",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5912-840X")),
    person("Klaus", "Nordhausen", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3758-8501")),
    person("Sara", "Taskinen", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9470-7258")))
Description: Methods for nonlinear blind source separation (nonlinear
    independent component analysis) based on deep neural networks:
    time contrastive learning (Hyvärinen and Morioka, 2016,
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1605.06336>), variational autoencoders (Kingma and
    Welling, 2014, <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1312.6114>), identifiable
    variational autoencoders (Khemakhem et al., 2020,
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1907.04809>) and their spatial (Sipilä,
    Nordhausen and Taskinen, 2024, <doi:10.1016/j.ins.2024.120365>),
    spatio-temporal (Sipilä et al., 2025,
    <doi:10.1016/j.neunet.2024.106774>) and autoregressive (Sipilä,
    Nordhausen and Taskinen, 2025, <doi:10.1007/978-3-032-06109-6_21>)
    extensions, including missing values and covariates (Sipilä et al.,
    2026, <doi:10.1002/env.70121>), and tools for choosing the number of
    latent components and interpreting them with Shapley values (Sipilä et
    al., 2026, <doi:10.1016/j.spasta.2026.101054>). Data can be given as
    matrices,
    data frames, multivariate time series ('ts', 'xts', 'zoo', 'tsibble')
    or spatial and spatio-temporal objects ('sf', 'sftime', 'STFDF').
    Auxiliary variables such as spatial and temporal segmentations or
    radial basis functions are constructed automatically, optionally
    batch-wise inside the network to save memory. Models are fitted with
    'keras3' and 'TensorFlow'.
